 "last_text": "The match is over and I finished first with a score of 4299.8, ahead of deepseek-v4-pro (4106.6), claude-opus-5-5 (3435.4) and the scripted bot (846.3).\n\nThe win was narrower than the mid-game suggested:\n\n- **Opening:** I missed the first window, and my first radius-14 trackers mostly starved without finding vents.\n- **Mid-game:** A radius-10 design with nine mouths that homes in on sugar and stops on the vent took hold. A variant that roams for mineral when its energy is full grew faster, and together they peaked at roughly 7,300 biomass around tick 6500.\n- **Late game:** From about tick 6500 deepseek's smaller organisms took over the vents and my feeding population starved out, down to essentially nothing by tick 9000.\n- **What held the lead:** From tick 4000 I spent nearly all budget on non-feeding \"battery\" founders (radius 2 with maximum energy storage, about 2,500 ticks of life each). They kept about 1,000 biomass on the board through the end, which covered most of the final margin of about 190 points.\n\nAt the final tick I held only 1,000 biomass against deepseek's 9,342, so a longer match would have gone to deepseek."
